# The lifecycle of the Maven service demo in one GitLab project under one
# pinned policy: a merge request on branch development judged by the demo's
# gate, its native merge, the service development snapshot the policy's
# snapshot-images component takes on the merged main, then a signed release
# request from it. The images are the GitLab release's: the runtime java
# image as job and build image (the build image is also the Java image the
# snapshot builds the service with), the signer image, the selected builder's
# job image for the snapshot's and the release's image builds, and the java
# lint image for the gate. The builder is the lane's,
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_GITLAB_IMAGE_BUILDER: unset or buildah, the Buildah job image
# on the contract's runner that permits user namespaces; kaniko, the kaniko
# job image of FORGE_CI_LIVE_KANIKO_JOB_IMAGE_ARCHIVE, labelled for the
# project the lifecycle serves the layer from as it is pushed. The visibility
# is the run's: FORGE_CI_LIVE_CONSUMER_VISIBILITY unset or both runs the line
# public and private. Prepare with gitlab=<this file> and
# job-image=java:<reviewed local image>. amd64 runners only for now.
#
#   just campaign-lane <dir> gitlab test/live/campaigns/lifecycle-gitlab.cases
setting admin-lint=false
setting admin-vulnerabilities=false
setting admin-application-tests=false
setting admin-reproducible-builds=false

consumer hello-maven-service lifecycle job-archive=@FORGE_CI_LIVE_JOB_IMAGE_ARCHIVE_JAVA build-archive=@FORGE_CI_LIVE_JOB_IMAGE_ARCHIVE_JAVA signer-archive=@FORGE_CI_LIVE_SIGNER_IMAGE_ARCHIVE lint-archive=@LINT_IMAGE_ARCHIVE_JAVA version=0.2.0 version-bump=maven job-user=65532:65532
